3. Textures
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Planet and satellite surface maps in assets/textures/ are downscaled crops of
public-domain imagery produced by NASA and USGS missions (e.g. Messenger,
Magellan / Pioneer Venus, MODIS Blue Marble, Mars Global Surveyor, Cassini,
Voyager 2, New Horizons, Galileo). They are included as-is (resized only) and
are credited to:

- NASA / JPL / USGS Astrogeology Science Center — public domain, see
  https://www.nasa.gov/media-guidelines/ and https://astroweb.usgs.gov/
- Solar System Scope (https://www.solarsystemscope.com/textures/) — CC BY 4.0,
  used for several planet maps.

Sky background:

- milkyway.webp — "The Milky Way panorama", ESO / S. Brunier, CC BY 4.0
  (https://www.eso.org/public/images/eso0932a/). Downscaled to 4096x2048
  equirectangular and re-encoded as WebP (quality 90). Used as the sky dome in
  assets/js/scene.js; the procedural star points are kept and overlaid on top,
  so the near-field star field is unchanged.

All maps above are stored as WebP (lossy, quality ~90) to shrink the embedded
payload; the original JPEG/PNG sources in assets/textures/ were replaced.

assets/js/textures.js is a generated artifact: the base64 encoding of the
files above, produced by scripts/generate-textures.js. It is committed so that
opening index.html over file:// works without a server. Do not hand-edit it.

Missing maps fall back to procedural rendering (solid color + shader detail);
no runtime error is produced.

