4. Astronomical data sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- JPL / NASA "Keplerian Elements for Approximate Positions of the Major Planets"
  (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/approx_pos.html) — J2000 elements, centennial
  rates and the outer-planet additional terms (b, c, s, f) used in
  assets/js/astro.js and assets/js/data.js.
- JPL "Planetary Satellite Mean Elements" (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/sats/elem/)
  — satellite mean elements (ascending node, argument of periapsis, mean
  anomaly) at epoch 2000-01-01.5 TDB, used for satellite orbit orientation
  in assets/js/data.js and assets/js/scene.js.
- IAU / IAU Minor Planet Center — dwarf-planet and comet elements (1P/Halley).
- NASA Planetary Fact Sheets (https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/)
  — radii, masses, gravity, density, escape velocity, temperatures.
- Milky Way structural parameters (R0 ≈ 8 kpc, bar ≈ 4.6 kpc, pitch ≈ 13°,
  flat rotation curve v ≈ 220 km/s) used in assets/js/galaxy.js follow published
  review values; the galaxy model is a stylized statistical model, not a
  catalog-based reconstruction.

Values are cross-checked but not guaranteed to survey precision. See
"Known limitations" in README.md.

